<article class="env-definition" id="01OQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01OQ">Definition <span data-tag="01OQ">28.4.2</span>.</a> Let $P$ be a property of rings. Let $X$ be a scheme. We say $X$ is <em>locally $P$</em> if for any $x \in X$ there exists an affine open neighbourhood $U$ of $x$ in $X$ such that $\mathcal{O}_ X(U)$ has property $P$. </p>
